From 50c02d3c6f101c101e05b7ad1b87e4d94d7bcf81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:51:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] fix(art): decide a card's localized printing ONCE, for
 every zone
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A card could render as two different printings at the same moment. Observed:
Seasoned Pyromancer showed as `2x2 #454` (Chinese) in hand and `2x2 #123`
(English) on the stack — the same spell, in the same frame, on the same screen.

The cause was that each entry point picked a printing for itself, at its own
moment, against state that loads lazily. `firstAvailablePrinting` returns null
until the availability set and the printings map have arrived, so an entry point
that resolved early silently kept the stored English printing while a later one
found the localized printing. Two async entry points, two answers.

Now the choice is made once per `oracle_id` for the whole session
(`canonicalPrintingIdFor`) and applied on every resolution path, so "which
printing is this card?" has exactly one answer rather than one per caller. A null
answer — this locale has no art for the card — is cached too, since that is a
property of the locale rather than of who asked.

The cache is cleared whenever the art locale changes: availability sets are
disjoint between locales, so a remembered printing would pin every card to one the
new locale may not have.

Measured over the pool: 15,718 cards resolve to a canonical printing, 3,544 have
no art in this locale and keep English art everywhere.
